From 2a18f85c2387d6d22548cfd5a87392eafcda501c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:08:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add single-radar mode and tolerate CH340 bit-7 corruption in
 data frames

With only one LD2410B connected, the daemon never counted anything: a car is
recorded only when radars A and B trigger in sequence. Add ld2410.mode
(auto|dual|single). Auto (default) switches to single-radar mode when only one
radar port is configured, or only one configured port exists at startup. In
single mode each rising edge counts as one car (cooldown + parked suppression),
recorded under the Inbound label since direction is unknown.

Also mask bit 7 on status/energy/distance-high bytes in basic data frames.
CH340 adapters at 256000 baud flip bit 7, which pushed energy above 100 and
silently dropped the frame.

Settings page: add 'None (single radar)' for Sensor B and a Radar Mode select.
Also read parked timeout from car.parked_timeout_s (what the UI saves).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ZE721391WYGMSx3qZprDn
