--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -159,6 +159,12 @@ SLED is a **production-grade prop controller** built by a Christmas lighting ent
 5. Parked cars suppress the car-event trigger until the car leaves
 6. All counts publish to MQTT and log to SQLite
 
+#### Single-radar mode
+
+Only have one LD2410B? Set **Sensor B Port** to *None (single radar)*, or set **Radar Mode** to *Single*. Every new detection on the one radar then counts as one car (after `car.cooldown_s`, or `ld2410.single_cooldown_s` if set), and parked suppression still applies. A single radar can't tell direction, so these counts are recorded under the `label_toward` (Inbound) label.
+
+`ld2410.mode` accepts `"auto"` (default), `"dual"` or `"single"`. In `auto`, the daemon uses single-radar mode when only one radar port is set, or when only one of the two configured ports exists at startup (for example, B is `/dev/ttyUSB1` but no second adapter is plugged in). Restart the plugin after plugging in a second radar.
+
 ---
 
 ## 🛠️ Hardware You'll Need
